# CR 608.2b: Get Out's second mode with two targets, one illegal as it resolves, still does what it can with the other. Bot1 targets both of its Ornithopters; in response Bot2's
# Lightning Bolt kills one (0/2), so only the other returns to Bot1's hand. The dead one is in the graveyard, not returned.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Get Out
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Get Out.Cast
Bot1.Modes(2)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1; Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Hand = Ornithopter; Island; Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Get Out; Ornithopter; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
